   "dist": "mcp",
   "doc": "api/mcp.shared.jsonrpc_dispatcher.md#peercancelmode",
   "inferred": "```xml <special-form 'Literal[\"interrupt\", \"signal\"]'> ``` --- How `notifications/cancelled` is applied: `\"interrupt\"` (default) cancels the handler's scope; `\"signal\"` only sets `ctx.cancel_requested` and lets the handler run to completion. Either way the cancelled request is never answered - the handler's eventual result or error is dropped, not written.",
   "inferred_by": "ty",
   "kind": "attribute",
   "labels": [
    "module-attribute"
   ],
   "name": "PeerCancelMode",
   "nameable": true,
   "path": "mcp.shared.jsonrpc_dispatcher.PeerCancelMode",
   "preferred": "mcp.shared.jsonrpc_dispatcher.PeerCancelMode",
   "signature": "PeerCancelMode = Literal['interrupt', 'signal']",
   "summary": "How `notifications/cancelled` is applied: `\"interrupt\"` (default) cancels the handler's scope; `\"signal\"` only sets `ctx.cancel_requested` and lets the handler run to completion. Either way the cancelled request is never answered - the han\u2026"
  },
